---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from '~/i18n/utils';

import Hero from '~/components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBand from '~/components/sections/TrustBand.astro';
import Ecosystem from '~/components/sections/Ecosystem.astro';
import SocialPlans from '~/components/sections/SocialPlans.astro';
import ContentShowcase from '~/components/sections/ContentShowcase.astro';
import EducationLibrary from '~/components/sections/EducationLibrary.astro';
import MolarTv from '~/components/sections/MolarTv.astro';
import GrowthStory from '~/components/sections/GrowthStory.astro';
import Testimonials from '~/components/sections/Testimonials.astro';
import Faq from '~/components/sections/Faq.astro';
import FinalCta from '~/components/sections/FinalCta.astro';

import { faqSchema, productSchema } from '~/data/schema';

/*
	The home page leads with MOLAR TV.

	The order used to follow the master strategy's own list — social media first,
	the waiting-room screen ten sections later. That is backwards as a sales
	argument. The screen is already on the wall, already switched on and already
	playing something worthless; MOLAR TV is the easiest yes on the site, and the
	library is the second. Social media is the upgrade once a practice is already
	publishing, not the way in.

	Five sections came off in the same pass, all of them re-telling the ecosystem
	the diagram already draws:

	  PatientJourney   the journey in six steps, which `Ecosystem` draws in one
	  WhyMolar         six blocks of prose making the case a fourth time
	  ProductSelector  a "pick your product" grid under a page that has already
	                   shown every product
	  ResourceHub      a wall of links off the page, at the point a visitor
	                   should be closer to checking out rather than further
	  GlobalReach /
	  GeoBand          two adjacent bands on the same languages-and-markets fact
	  ClientProof      grids of published posts, immediately above CustomerStories
	                   doing the same. Its own header says it exists BECAUSE the
	                   strategy wanted a logo wall and there was no art for one —
	                   and there is now, sixteen real marks in `TrustBand`. So the
	                   breadth argument is made once, in logos, and the depth
	                   argument once, in `CustomerStories`, which carries the
	                   measured results this never did.

	They all still exist and still run on their own pages. Nothing was deleted —
	the home page just stopped saying everything four times.

	Two things here the strategy's section list does not name, both deliberate:

	  Faq         it is linked from the Resources menu as /#faq, and netlify.toml
	              redirects /faq to that fragment. The FAQPage structured data
	              below is generated from the same array the section renders, so
	              the two cannot drift.
	  productSchema  the plans are on this page with their prices visible, so
	              Product/Offer markup describes something a visitor can see.
*/
const locale = getLocale(Astro);
const t = useTranslations(locale);
---

<BaseLayout
	title={t('pages.homeTitle')}
	description={t('pages.homeDesc')}
	ogImage={{
		src: '/images/og/home.png',
		alt: 'MOLAR — the content engine for modern dental practices',
		width: 1200,
		height: 630,
	}}
	type="website"
	transparentNav
	schema={[productSchema(locale), faqSchema()]}
>
	{/*
		Order is the argument, and the argument changed.

		It used to open on social media and reach the waiting-room screen ten
		sections later. That is backwards: the screen is the thing a practice
		already owns and is already wasting, MOLAR TV is what should be playing on
		it, and it is the easiest yes on this page. Social is the upgrade once the
		content is already running.

		So: the hook, then proof it is real, then the two products you start with,
		then the ecosystem ONCE, then the price, then who says so.

		The ecosystem used to be told four times over — the diagram, the journey,
		the six blocks and the selector. `Ecosystem` is the one that draws it, and
		it is the one that stays.
	*/}
	<Hero />
	<MolarTv />
	<TrustBand />
	<ContentShowcase />
	<GrowthStory />
	<Ecosystem />
	<SocialPlans />
	<EducationLibrary />
	<Testimonials />
	<Faq />
	<FinalCta />
</BaseLayout>
